  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>w</mi></math> be two complex numbers such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Re</mo><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;has minimum value. Then, the minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math> for which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></math> is real, is equal to _______."
  },
